 ## Subtopics
 
 ### HSV Hue Color Mapping
-Maps scalar values to hue in the HSV color model to allow lighting effects on saturation and value while keeping hue invertible [S2]. It uses a simple linear function to map scalar values from range $[v_{min}, v_{max}]$ to hue range $[H_{min}, H_{max}]$ [S2]. For emphasizing a specific value $v_d$, it provides a wider color spectrum for an interval close to $v_d$ [S2]. In vector field visualization on isosurfaces, it maps streamline color to hues based on direction (inflow/outflow) and magnitude [S2]. Unlike the smoothstep-based Hue Transfer Function, this variant operates directly in HSV space, decoupling hue from lighting-induced saturation/value changes [S2].
