 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per sample. The calculation involves a fixed number of arithmetic operations and smoothstep evaluations.
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$. No lookup tables or auxiliary data structures are required.
-- **Strengths:** Procedural generation avoids memory overhead of large LUTs. The smoothstep approach ensures C1 continuity between color bands, avoiding harsh discontinuities common in simple piecewise linear RGB mapping.
-- **Limitations:** The color palette is fixed to the specific 6-segment cycle defined by the formula. It does not support arbitrary color ranges without modifying the coefficients.
-- **When to use:** When a compact, procedural spectral palette is needed for volume rendering or scalar field visualization, and memory bandwidth is a constraint.
-- **When not to use:** When specific, non-spectral colors are required, or when the input data range does not map naturally to the $[0, 1]$ hue cycle.
