 ## Background
-The Hue Transfer Function is derived from procedural color generation techniques used in computer graphics, specifically those involving smooth interpolation between primary and secondary colors. The specific formulation using `smoothstep` differences for RGB channels is documented in the `terier/vpt` repository [S1, unofficial]. The concept of mapping scalars to HSV hue for visualization, particularly for preserving invertibility under lighting, is discussed in the context of adaptive multi-valued volume data visualization [S2].
